From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui, gridcraft-web: a read-only workbook is refused before anything is drawn changed

docs/phase5/r6.md, owner 2026-11-08: the R6 bridge let an edit of a read-only workbook happen and took it back in the next frame,
so typed text showed for a frame. Now the editor and the bridge stop it before anything is drawn changed: the bridge sets
`Session::read_only` (gridcraft/0161) at every frame and on open; `begin_edit` (typing, F2, double-click, the formula bar,
Backspace), the text box editor, the header and footer editor, and the drags that change the workbook (fill handle, move by the
border, column and row resize, column move, freeze handles, chart/picture/shape move and resize) refuse to start and show the
existing read-only message as a toast (no modal per key press); a command the engine refuses shows the same toast. The per-frame
revert stays as the last resort and logs `read-only safety net` when it fires. New `SheetApp::read_only_notice` carries the
translated message (the host sets it); no new UI string.
---

diff --git a/apps/gridcraft-web/src/host.rs b/apps/gridcraft-web/src/host.rs
index a3fa584a..992ebb59 100644
--- a/apps/gridcraft-web/src/host.rs
+++ b/apps/gridcraft-web/src/host.rs
@@ -149,7 +149,10 @@ impl Bridge {
     /// for, take back edits of a read-only workbook, and report the unsaved-changes state. True
     /// while a plugin call waits for the page (the caller keeps drawing frames).
     pub fn sync(&self, app: &mut SheetApp) -> bool {
+        // Read only is the engine's own state: it refuses every command that changes the workbook, and the editors do not open.
+        app.session.read_only = self.read_only.get();
         if let Some((name, bytes)) = self.to_open.borrow_mut().take() {
+            app.read_only_notice = app.ui.language.tr(READ_ONLY).to_string();
             self.open(app, name, &bytes);
         }
         if self.save_requested.replace(false) && !self.read_only.get() {
@@ -184,11 +187,12 @@ impl Bridge {
                 doc.saved = Arc::new((*doc.wb).clone());
             }
         }
-        // Read only: whatever changed the workbook (a command, typing, a drag) is taken back, as Undo would.
+        // Read only: the engine and the editors refuse edits before they happen; this takes back whatever got through anyway.
         if self.read_only.get()
             && let Some(doc) = app.session.active_mut()
             && doc.is_dirty()
         {
+            log::warn!("read-only safety net: the workbook changed and was taken back");
             doc.wb = doc.saved.clone();
             doc.calc.rebuild(&doc.wb);
             doc.undo.clear();
